Example of a good tip:
{"title": "Airbrushing Vallejo Model Color — The 1:1 Rule", "text": "Vallejo Model Color is thicker than Model Air and needs thinning for airbrushing. Mix at a 1:1 ratio with Vallejo Airbrush Thinner (71.261) for a baseline consistency. Add 2-3 drops of Vallejo Flow Improver (71.262) per 10 drops of thinned paint to prevent tip dry on fine nozzle setups (0.2mm needle). Spray at 1.0-1.5 bar pressure. Test on a white plastic spoon — if the paint spiders outward, add more thinner; if it splatters like sandpaper texture, reduce pressure or add flow improver."}

