prompts.TROUBLESHOOTING_PROTIPS:
Generate 5 practical scale model building tips about TROUBLESHOOTING & PRO TIPS. Cover topics like: fixing silvered decals, removing old paint from kits, fixing broken photo-etch parts, recovering clogged airbrushes, repairing warped parts, avoiding frost from rattle cans, fixing paint reactions/bubbling, and stripping badly painted models. Mention specific brands like Tamiya, Vallejo, AK Interactive, Microscale, Clear Prop Models, Mr. Hobby, Iwata, Arma Hobby, ICM, Eduard.

Example of a good tip:
{"title": "Fixing Silvered Decals After They Have Dried", "text": "Silvered decals (visible silver film around markings) happen when air is trapped under the decal. To fix after drying: apply Mr. Mark Softer (or Micro Sol) generously over the decal, wait 10 minutes, then press gently with a damp cotton swab from the center outward to force air bubbles out. Repeat twice more with fresh solution. If silvering persists, carefully slit the decal film with a new #11 blade in a crosshatch pattern, apply setting solution again, and press flat. Once fully settled, seal with a gloss coat. For stubborn cases, replace the decal and reapply with stronger solutions like Daco Strong."}

